**Day 41: Introduction to Server-side Development**  

**Topic:**  
Understanding the difference between server-side and client-side development, the request-response cycle, and HTTP basics (GET/POST methods).  

**Learning Objectives:**  

• Differentiate between server-side and client-side processing  
• Explain the HTTP request-response cycle  
• Identify GET and POST methods in web interactions  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  

• Draw a client-server architecture diagram using Draw.io  
• Analyze 5 websites to identify server-side vs. client-side components  
• Research and document common HTTP methods  

**Important Concepts:**  

• Server-side processes execute on the web server  
• Client-side processes run in the user's browser  
• GET requests retrieve data, POST requests submit data  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  

• Not applicable for this introductory session  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  

• E-commerce sites processing payments (server-side)  
• Form validations before submission (client-side)  

**Tools / Tech:**  

• Draw.io for architecture diagrams  
• Web browser developer tools  
• Postman (for future API testing)  

**Summary:**  
Today introduced fundamental server-side concepts including the client-server model and HTTP methods. Students practiced visualizing architectures and identifying real-world implementations.  

